 r"I am writing to apply for the Graduate Management Consultant position in the Business Advisory team at Arcadis. I completed an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London in September 2026, where a distinction is expected, after a BSc in Biological Sciences at Imperial College London, and I currently work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK. Across my academic and professional experience I have gathered and interpreted data, turned it into recommendations for clients and colleagues, and used digital tools to change how teams work.",

 r"What attracts me most to Business Advisory is that the work has a visible end point: transformation and digital solutions that improve outcomes for people, the planet and profit across infrastructure, utilities and the built environment. The posting describes supporting business transformation, gathering and interpreting data, preparing client presentations and supporting workshops, which is the mix of analysis and client work I enjoy most, and I am particularly interested in the Digital \& AI capability. I like taking an unclear problem, identifying what clients actually need, and turning it into a workflow that can be tested and improved.",

 r"At TikTok Shop UK I analyse merchant and transaction data in SQL and Python and build the KPI frameworks and dashboards that operations, product and commercial teams use to set targets and track initiatives. When my supervisor asked me to configure a campaign for merchants by hand, I worked through a few examples, saw the underlying logic and used Claude Code to build a multi-step agent with a validation step to check its own output, which cut the time the task took by around 40 to 50 percent. Persuading a sceptical colleague that it was accurate mattered as much as building it, and it taught me that change only sticks once the people affected trust it.",

 r"At DS Digital Technology I worked as a Data Scientist Intern on a healthcare AI project for a pharmaceutical client. I worked with the client's clinical experts to turn their requirements into a benchmark and rubric that the client adopted as its acceptance standard, built the Python pipeline that tested the product against it, and presented the findings and risks to clinical and business stakeholders. It showed me how much of consulting is agreeing what good looks like with the client before any analysis begins.",

 r"At Ipsos Strategy3 I researched emerging health-product markets, structured data from more than 80 healthcare professional interviews, built market-sizing models and presented recommendations to client teams. My MSc dissertation used data from 458,840 UK Biobank participants and was delivered as an interactive tool for non-specialists. Both taught me to organise complex information clearly and present it to an audience who wants the implication rather than the method.",

 r"I would bring Arcadis strong analytical and data skills, practical experience of client delivery and digital transformation, and the habit of explaining technical work clearly to the people who will act on it. I have the right to work in the UK until January 2029 without sponsorship. I am based in London, happy to travel to client sites, and available to start in 2027.",

